  "readme": "## california__swap-2025__README.md\n# California State Wildlife Action Plan (SWAP) 2025\n\nCloud-native mirror of the finalized **California SWAP 2025** (CDFW, adopted\nOctober 2025) spatial framework, species ranges, and conservation\ntarget/strategy tables, under `s3://public-swap/california/swap-2025/`.\n\n> SWAP 2025 supersedes the SWAP 2015 companion layers previously published here;\n> the 2015 raw sources remain under `public-cdfw/raw/swap-2015-*` for reference.\n\n## Collections\n\n**Spatial layers** (GeoParquet + PMTiles + H3 hex at resolution 8):\n\n| Collection | `source-layer` / path | Features | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Provinces | `provinces` | 8 | adds an **Anadromous** province vs. 2015's 7 |\n| Conservation Units | `conservation-units` | 46 | `ConsUnitType`: Terrestrial / Freshwater Aquatic / Marine / Anadromous |\n| SGCN Species Ranges (v4) | `sgcn-ranges` | 422 | species range polygons |\n| Marine Bioregions | `marine-bioregions` | 3 | reference geography |\n| NOAA ESU/DPS | `noaa-esu-dps` | 37 | anadromous salmonid units |\n| Bay-Delta Conservation Unit | `bay-delta-conservation-unit` | 1 | reference geography |\n\n**Non-spatial tables** (Parquet):\n\n| Collection | path | Rows |\n|---|---|---|\n| Conservation Targets | `targets` | 460 |\n| Conservation Strategies | `strategies` | 525 |\n| SGCN Species list | `sgcn-species` | 1,437 |\n| SGCN Species \u00d7 Conservation Unit | `sgcn-species-units` | 4,268 |\n\nPublic base URL: `https://s3-west.nrp-nautilus.io/public-swap/california/swap-2025/`\n\n## Data model (joins)\n\n```\nProvinces.ProvinceID \u2500\u2500< ConservationUnits.ParentProvinceID\nConservationUnits.Name \u2500\u2500< Targets.ConsUnit         (also Targets.Province)\nTargets.TargetID \u2500\u2500< Strategies.ParentTargetID\nSpecies.SpeciesKey \u2500\u2500< SgcnRanges.ParentSpeciesKey\nSgcnSpeciesUnits.ConUnit \u2192 ConservationUnits.Name   (after name normalization)\n# SgcnSpeciesUnits.ParentProvSpeciesKey does NOT join to Species.SpeciesKey --\n# it indexes a separate species-by-province table that CDFW has not published.\n```\n\n## MapLibre GL JS (PMTiles)\n\nThe MapLibre **`source-layer` is the last path segment** (`provinces`,\n`conservation-units`, `sgcn-ranges`, \u2026), not the source service name.\n\n```js\nimport { Protocol } from \"pmtiles\";\nconst protocol = new Protocol();\nmaplibregl.addProtocol(\"pmtiles\", protocol.tile);\n\nmap.addSource(\"cu\", {\n  type: \"vector\",\n  url: \"pmtiles://https://s3-west.nrp-nautilus.io/public-swap/california/swap-2025/conservation-units.pmtiles\",\n});\nmap.addLayer({\n  id: \"cu-fill\", type: \"fill\", source: \"cu\",\n  \"source-layer\": \"conservation-units\",       // <-- last segment of the dataset\n  paint: {\n    \"fill-color\": [\"match\", [\"get\", \"ConsUnitType\"],\n      \"Marine\", \"#2c7fb8\", \"Freshwater Aquatic\", \"#41b6c4\",\n      \"Anadromous\", \"#7fcdbb\", \"Terrestrial\", \"#31a354\", \"#cccccc\"],\n    \"fill-opacity\": 0.5, \"fill-outline-color\": \"#333\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## DuckDB\n\n```sql\nINSTALL spatial; LOAD spatial;\n\n-- Conservation units by type\nSELECT ConsUnitType, COUNT(*) FROM read_parquet(\n  'https://s3-west.nrp-nautilus.io/public-swap/california/swap-2025/conservation-units.parquet')\nGROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC;\n\n-- Targets + their strategies for one conservation unit\nSELECT t.ConsUnit, t.TargetHab, s.Action\nFROM read_parquet('https://s3-west.nrp-nautilus.io/public-swap/california/swap-2025/targets.parquet') t\nJOIN read_parquet('https://s3-west.nrp-nautilus.io/public-swap/california/swap-2025/strategies.parquet') s\n  ON s.ParentTargetID = t.TargetID\nWHERE t.ConsUnit = 'Klamath Mountains';\n\n-- SGCN species (with mapped range) in a taxonomic group\nSELECT SWAP_Common, SWAP_Scientific\nFROM read_parquet('https://s3-west.nrp-nautilus.io/public-swap/california/swap-2025/sgcn-ranges.parquet')\nWHERE Taxonomic_Group = 'Amphibians'\nORDER BY SWAP_Common;\n```\n\n### H3 hex\n\nSpatial layers carry `h8` (native resolution 8) and `h0` (partition key), one\nrow per (feature, cell) pair. **`Shape__Area`/`Shape__Length` are per-feature\ntotals repeated on every hex cell \u2014 never `SUM` them on hex**; for coverage area\nuse `SUM(h3_cell_area(h8, 'km^2'))` over the distinct cells (H3 cells are not equal area, so a per-resolution constant is not a substitute). `_cng_fid`/`h8`/`h0` are\nsafe keys.\n\n## Provenance & license\n\n- **Source:** CDFW BIOS / ArcGIS (org `Uq9r85Potqm3MfRV`), services\n  `SWAP_target_strategy_v3_gdb`, `SWAP_SGCN_V4_gdb`, `SWAP_Reference_Layers_WFL1`,\n  paginated from their FeatureServers to GeoJSON (the Hub `downloads/data` export\n  is not enabled for these services).\n- **Plan:** [California State Wildlife Action Plan 2025](https://wildlife.ca.gov/SWAP/Final)\n  (finalized October 2025).\n- **License:** CC-BY-4.0 (CDFW attribution terms). Attribute the California\n  Department of Fish and Wildlife.\n",
